13:T659,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How does the wheel-to-ski conversion work on the Gravity Cart Sport?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The GC-SPORT-01 chassis mounts its terrain interface at the same certified attachment points year-round. Swapping to winter use means releasing the wheel assembly and engaging the Ski Assembly Kit (GC-SKI-200) — a tool-free binding, no separate frame."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What terrain and grade is the ski conversion rated for?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The GC-SKI-200 ski assembly is 780mm in length and rated to a 25% descent grade on packed snow, fitted to the GC-SPORT-01 chassis."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What braking hardware does the Gravity Cart Sport use?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Shimano Dual Brake Kit (GC-BRK-180) is a hydraulic dual-disc set with 180mm front and rear rotors, tested against the ECE R100 braking standard."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the load rating of the certified chassis?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The GC-SPORT-01 chassis is rated to 120kg, with certified wheel and ski assemblies included, engineered for pavement, gravel and packed snow."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the Gravity Cart Sport CE and ISO compliant?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The Gravity Cart Sport is independently tested and documented against ECE 2006/42/EG, ISO EN 12100 and ISO EN 4210 — the same category of machinery and safety directives that govern the automotive and machinery industries."}}]}8:["$","main",null,{"className":"mx-auto min-h-screen max-w-3xl px-6 py-24","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BlogPosting\",\"headline\":\"Crashed a Fork or Worn Out a Rotor? You Replace the Part, Not the Cart\",\"description\":\"GC-SPORT-01 owners can buy the stainless fork, brake kit or ski assembly as standalone certified parts — no proprietary lock-in, no full-chassis replacement after a crash or wear.\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-09-19\",\"url\":\"https://1bf88dc5.run.linkworld.ai/blog/2026-09-19-replacing-a-single-component\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"GravityCart\"}}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Product\",\"sku\":\"GC-SPORT-01\",\"name\":\"Gravity Cart Sport\",\"description\":\"The flagship convertible chassis. Certified wheel and ski assemblies included — one machine, engineered for pavement, gravel and packed snow.\",\"url\":\"https://1bf88dc5.run.linkworld.ai/product\",\"additionalProperty\":[{\"@type\":\"PropertyValue\",\"name\":\"Rated load\",\"value\":\"120kg\"},{\"@type\":\"PropertyValue\",\"name\":\"Fork material\",\"value\":\"Stainless steel fork\"},{\"@type\":\"PropertyValue\",\"name\":\"Brakes\",\"value\":\"Shimano dual disc brakes\"},{\"@type\":\"PropertyValue\",\"name\":\"Certifications\",\"value\":\"CE, ISO\"}],\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"priceCurrency\":\"EUR\",\"price\":\"2890.00\",\"availability\":\"https://schema.org/InStock\",\"url\":\"https://1bf88dc5.run.linkworld.ai/product\"}}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$13"}}],["$","$L14",null,{"href":"/blog","className":"underline opacity-70","children":"← All posts"}],"$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18"]}]
15:["$","h1",null,{"className":"mt-8 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight","children":"Crashed a Fork or Worn Out a Rotor? You Replace the Part, Not the Cart"}]
16:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm opacity-60","children":"2026-09-19"}]
19:Ta4e,<p>A question we hear from owners and dealers alike, usually after a hard landing or a season of hard use: &quot;I bent the fork / burned through a rotor — do I need to send back the whole cart?&quot;</p>
<p>No. The GC-SPORT-01 was engineered as a serviceable machine, not a sealed unit, and every wear or crash-prone assembly on it is sold as a standalone, certified part.</p>
<h2>What&#39;s actually replaceable</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Stainless Steel Fork (GC-FRK-100)</strong> — 304 stainless, 42mm rake, tool-free quick-release mount. If a fork takes a direct hit in a crash, this is the part that&#39;s designed to absorb it, and the part you replace — not the chassis behind it.</li>
<li><strong>Shimano Dual Brake Kit (GC-BRK-180)</strong> — the hydraulic dual-disc set, 180mm rotors front and rear, ECE R100 tested. Rotors and pads wear with use like any braking system; this kit is sold complete so a replacement goes back on tested to the same standard as the original, not a mismatched aftermarket substitute.</li>
<li><strong>Ski Assembly Kit (GC-SKI-200)</strong> — sold independently of the fork and brake kit, this is the same certified conversion kit described in <a href="/blog/2026-09-02-gravity-powered-descent-carts">how the chassis converts between modes</a>, available on its own if you&#39;re re-equipping a chassis for winter or replacing a damaged ski assembly.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Why we sell parts, not just carts</h2>
<p>This follows directly from how the chassis itself is built: a mono-material 6061-T6 aluminum frame chosen in part because it&#39;s straightforward to repair with regionally sourced hardware, not a proprietary structure that forces a factory return. The fork, brake kit and ski assembly are the same logic applied to the wear components — each one mounts to the same certified attachment points as the original, at the same torque specs, so a replacement part restores the chassis to its original 120kg-rated certification rather than degrading it.</p>
<p>A cart that can only be repaired by the factory isn&#39;t a seasonal vehicle you own for years — it&#39;s a single-use product with a long warranty. We built the opposite.</p>
<h2>Getting the right part</h2>
<p>If you&#39;re not sure which component failed or which kit your chassis needs, check the part number stamped near the mount point against the specification exhibits above — each part on GravityCart.com is listed under its own part number (GC-FRK-100, GC-BRK-180, GC-SKI-200) for exactly this reason.</p>
<p><strong><a href="/product">Order the certified replacement part for your GC-SPORT-01 →</a></strong></p>
